      {
        "id": 225731,
        "name": "dpt",
        "username": "dpt",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-02-23T12:10:19.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ras906\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ras906/48/1956_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> ras906:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I’m sure this is answered somewhere else but if there is 1 badland in an area and you do 1 damage to 2 different towns in that area, does the badland do 1 more damage to each town and destroy both towns?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>To amplify what Paul said, you would end up destroying 1 Town and leaving the other with 1 damage.</p>\n<p>Each Badlands does 1 extra damage per “Action”, which is a term that will be carefully defined in the Jagged Earth rules; this includes one Spirit Power, for instance.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:59:27.149Z",
